ills. Concerns: grumpy, uncooperative (crew cooperation).\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. Strengths: anticipation, complex understanding, spatial vision, leadership. Concerns: takes criticism poorly, unorganized (reliability?).\n\nCandidate D: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as arrogant, weak leadership, arrogant (crew cooperation). Strengths: problem solving, concentration, responsibility. Concerns: arrogance, weak leadership.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely candidate B has strong stress resilience and conscientiousness, but uncooperative may be big issue. Candidate C has strong technical competence and leadership but poor criticism handling and unorganized may affect reliability. Candidate D strong problem solving and responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership. Candidate A reliability and decision speed but communication issues and egocentric.\n\nWhich is best? Long-distance pilot requires reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility. Candidate B seems strong on stress, conscientiousness (reliability), but uncooperative is a serious crew cooperation issue. Candidate C strong technical, anticipation, leadership, but unorganized and poor at criticism may affect reliability and cooperation. Candidate D strong problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but arrogance and weak leadership affect crew cooperation. Candidate A reliability, decision speed, positive atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation and professional communication.\n\nWe need to weigh. Perhaps Candidate C's technical competence and leadership outweigh unorganized? But unorganized could affect reliability. Candidate B's uncooperative is a red flag for crew cooperation. Candidate D's arrogance also a red flag. Candidate A's communication difficulty is also a red flag.\n\nThus maybe Candidate C is best overall despite some concerns. Let's propose recommendation for Candidate C, but we need to justify with facts.\n\nWe should also note that we haven't yet discussed all candidates, but we can still give provisional recommendation. According to process, we should still cover all candidates before final, but we can give provisional vote.\n\nThus: I will state my current recommendation is Candidate C, because of anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, which align with technical competence, decision quality, responsibility. Acknowledge concerns: criticism and organization, but may be mitigated.\n\nLet's produce public message."}
